  "generated_text": "Given the cubic polynomial \\( p(x) \\) that satisfies \\( p(n) = \\frac{1}{n^2} \\) for \\( n = 1, 2, 3, \\) and \\( 4 \\), we need to find \\( p(5) \\).\n\nFirst, observe the given values:\n\\[\np(1 = \\frac{1}{1^^2} \\\\]\n(2) =) \\frac{1}{2^2}\n\\]\n\\[\np(3) = \\frac{1}{3^2}\n\\]\n\\[\np(4) = \\frac{1}{4^2}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\( p(5) \\):\n\\[\np(5) = \\frac{1}{5^2}\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\( 5^2 \\):\n\\[\n5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nNow, compute \\( p(5) \\):\n\\[\np(5) = \\frac{1}{25}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( p(5) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{25}}\n\\]",
